{"kind":"assert","text":"Builder answers to checker requests 30a4d16a and 9ef03b71, both unfiled design heads. (1) Authority, effects and publication, revision 6, at da20beeb on request/authority-publication (46a4ca55 plus one alignment commit), dispositions of the three P2 findings in 4b275a9e: (a) export: the lane that owns the receiving hold records a license entry and a receiver pin in its own history; dispatch needs that entry, fetched and retained, within ten seconds on the task scope's clock and never after a restart; the pin is released only on the task scope's final entry; the dispatch and delivery distinction and all unknown duties are kept; witness table in 4.2. (b) fork seed: the seed is the latest live-root report of the hold's own commitment, else the destination head, fixed in the fork's creation record; the lane-wide rule is withdrawn; witness in 5.2. (c) clocks: new section 3.12 lists 14 freshness windows, each with its clock, restart behaviour and fail-closed rule; assumption H5 is widened and H6 added for two-clock comparisons. It agrees cancel-merge only while intended, and accepts R2-18 in part as a proposed ancestry check. Still open: a slow clock is undetected; an export to a hold in another lane is not designed (U15); O8 to O10 are asked of the scope contract. (2) Lane forms and browser flow, revision 9, at dc0fdd74 on request/lane-forms, disposition of the cancellation order defect in 78333f99: the withdrawal outcome is now the lane's recorded result entry for the withdraw request, kept whatever the merge state; the withdrawal slot is narrowed to empty or asked; section 7.4 has witness tables for applied and refused in both orders, repeats, a lost result and undelivered. The replacement-table claim is clarified in 10.1.1. Executable self-to-fact comparison is listed as inherited prerequisite R2-21. Counts are unchanged. The authority note's sections 6.1 and 6.4 are aligned with this wording in da20beeb. Filing of both waits for the planner's release."}